# OpenBao operational assets are executed on Linux and must remain LF-normalized.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
ops/openbao/policy/*.hcl text eol=lf
ops/openbao/staging/*.sh text eol=lf
ops/openbao/staging/*.py text eol=lf
ops/openbao/staging/*.md text eol=lf
scripts/openbao-operator-backup-static-check.mjs text eol=lf
# Compliance secret-hygiene gate is a shebang .mjs parsed by Vitest/oxc; a CRLF
# checkout (Windows autocrlf) breaks parsing. Force LF on every platform.
scripts/security/check-env-example.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/security/__tests__/check-env-example.test.mjs text eol=lf
# Same hazard, same remedy: the dependency-audit gate is a shebang .mjs imported
# by two Vitest suites, and its committed blob is LF. Without this pin a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf) stores it CRLF and both suites collect zero tests while
# CI keeps enforcing the gate. vitest.config.ts neutralises the shebang as well.
scripts/ci/dependency-audit-gate.mjs text eol=lf

# PHASE 104 — the Figma visual-system plugin is fingerprinted by RAW BYTES.
#
# `build.mjs` records sha256 over the plugin's own sources and over dist/, and
# three tests in `scripts/test-dna.mjs` re-hash the checked-out files and compare
# against `dist/build-report.json`. Those hashes are byte identities, not text
# comparisons, so any end-of-line conversion changes them.
#
# The committed blobs are LF: `dist/code.js` hashes to
# 78c59d65e0df783a2d343345334f44c91e5b0581d62f6a7dd82d50c9d3eb8de7, exactly the
# value `build-report.json` expects. With `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout
# rewrites 2827 line endings and the same, provably correct, artifact hashes to
# 135007f1550077fec79687f6d374bbc9145ab1bacdd6b2d009b12dc120333d1f — a red test
# on a green artifact. Pinning the directory to LF makes the checkout byte-exact
# on every platform. It is a no-op on Linux and on CI, where nothing converted
# anything in the first place.
#
# The fix is here rather than in the tests on purpose: relaxing a byte identity
# to a text comparison would retire the only check that can catch a tampered or
# stale plugin bundle.
tools/figma/hermes-phase104-visual-system/** text eol=lf

# S0-B-05 — the deterministic Prisma failure-semantics inventory is verified by
# sha256 over its rendered bytes, and the scanner that renders it is a shebang
# .mjs run by `node --test`.
#
# The inventory's committed blob is LF and hashes to
# 0fea9170b4db4f592defca15e0c3fb2cd81940c36f7159a45b9535218c48047e, which is the
# value `check` compares against. With `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout
# rewrites every line ending, so the same, provably correct, file hashes to a
# different value and the gate turns red on an unchanged artifact. The scanner
# also reads its own fixtures and computes `sourceFingerprint` over raw bytes,
# so a CRLF checkout would stale every one of the 187 manual adjudications, 268
# edge traces and 69 residual screenings at once.
#
# Pinning to LF makes the checkout byte-exact on every platform; it is a no-op on
# Linux and on CI, where nothing converted anything to begin with.
/docs/security/GETPRISMA-FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.md text eol=lf
/docs/security/s0-getprisma-callsite-inventory.json text eol=lf
/scripts/security/s0/** text eol=lf

# S0-B-03 — the edge/origin evidence document is identified by the sha256 of its
# bytes in the S0 closure report (0d44a6c2…). `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite
# every line ending on a fresh Windows checkout and change that hash without an
# edit, so the evidence would stop reproducing. Same hazard, same remedy as the
# B-05 artifacts above.
/docs/security/EDGE-ORIGIN-AND-CLIENT-IP.md text eol=lf

# S1 — the risk register is verified by the sha256 of its bytes, the report's
# generated blocks are compared byte for byte against what the checker renders,
# and the checker is a dependency-free .mjs run by `node --test`. With
# `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout would rewrite every line ending and
# break all three comparisons on files nobody edited. Same hazard, same remedy as
# the S0 artifacts above.
/docs/security/THREAT-MODEL-AND-RISK-REGISTER.md text eol=lf
/docs/security/s1-risk-register.json text eol=lf
/scripts/security/s1/risk-register-check.mjs text eol=lf
/scripts/security/s1/__tests__/risk-register.selftest.mjs text eol=lf
